Hey there,

I installed Xenomai 2.5.2 with Linux 2.6.31.4 kernel (ubuntu 9.10).
Everything seemed to work just fine. However, after inserting the PEAK PCI
can bus card the Xenomai kernel stopped booting while normal kernels
(non-xenomai) still boot.

I am running a 64 bit dell precision workstation (T7500) with 8 cores and a
NVIDIA 4800 FX. The attached text file contains the output of lspci -vvv
-nn.

I followed the install instruction for Xenomai 2.5.2 as posted here
http://wiki.barrett.com/support/wiki/InstallXenomai25

Unfortunately, I have no idea how to debug this problem. I have the
"feeling" that it has to do with the APIC and the way interrupts are
assigned.

Attached is also 2 syslogs of failed boots. I really hope that someone can
make sense out of them or at least can give me some hints on how to trace
down the problem.

I recompiled Xenomai with linux 2.6.31.8 with the adeos patch provided by
Xenomai, but still, I got the same trouble.

Thanks,
 peter

